### 2. Business Process Graph Service ✅

**File:** `/services/normalization-engine/src/enrichment/business_process_service.py` (580 lines)

**Features:**
- Asset-to-process mapping (TimescaleDB queries)
- Process criticality calculation (0.0 - 1.0)
- Crown jewel identification (tier = 1)
- LRU caching (1-hour TTL, 10,000 max size)
- Cache statistics tracking
- Database connection pooling

**Query Example:**
```sql
SELECT DISTINCT
    bp.id AS process_id,
    bp.name AS process_name,
    bp.process_type,
    bp.tier
FROM business_process_graph bpg
CROSS JOIN LATERAL jsonb_array_elements(bpg.nodes) AS node
JOIN LATERAL jsonb_to_record(node) AS bp(
    id TEXT,
    name TEXT,
    type TEXT,
    hostname TEXT,
    ip_address TEXT,
    process_type TEXT,
    tier INT
) ON TRUE
WHERE bpg.customer_id = $1
  AND (bp.hostname = ANY($2) OR bp.ip_address = ANY($2) OR bp.id = ANY($2))
ORDER BY bp.tier ASC, bp.name ASC;
```

**Criticality Calculation:**
- Tier score: 40% weight (Crown Jewel = 1.0, Critical = 0.8, etc.)
- Downtime cost: 30% weight (normalized to $1M max)
- Dependent processes: 20% weight (normalized to 100 max)
- Confidence: 10% weight

**Cache Performance:**
- Target hit rate: >90%
- TTL: 1 hour (configurable)
- Max size: 10,000 entries

